; Sift — fennec's typed-data toolkit: ONE shape language ['a Sift.t] that says what a value IS, and
; from it drives BSON encode/decode, validation, plain + extended JSON I/O, structural diff for reactive
; sync, DDP method arguments, and $jsonSchema reflection. Built ON Bson.t (the tree the storage layer
; already speaks) — simple to reason about, no neutral data model, no format abstraction. Pure +
; jsoo-safe, so the SAME codec runs on the server and in the browser. The Mongo query vocabulary is the
; companion fennec.pulse.sift.mongo; the [@@deriving] DX is fennec.pulse.sift.ppx. Neither is needed to
; use a codec.

(library
 (name sift)
 (public_name fennec.pulse.sift)
 (libraries fennec-mongo.bson fennec-mongo.bson_json fennec-mongo.json base64))
